# RD-Agent configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (in the repo root) and fill in your own keys.
# The file is git-ignored (`.env*` rule), so your keys never leave this machine.
#
# Two validated setups are provided below:
#   * Setup A (recommended): chat + embedding on different providers.
#     Chat goes through any OpenAI-compatible gateway via the `deepseek/`
#     provider variables (DEEPSEEK_API_BASE / DEEPSEEK_API_KEY), embedding
#     goes to SiliconFlow (or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) via the
#     `litellm_proxy/` variables. The two variable sets are fully isolated.
#   * Setup B: everything (chat + embedding) on a single provider that
#     hosts both kinds of models (e.g. SiliconFlow).
#
# IMPORTANT pitfalls learned in production (see DEPLOYMENT.md for details):
#   * Do NOT set OPENAI_API_BASE / OPENAI_API_KEY when using the
#     `litellm_proxy/` prefix: litellm lets the generic OPENAI_* variables
#     hijack the litellm_proxy route (both base and key), which silently
#     breaks the embedding calls.
#   * A stale-but-present (even empty) OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL
#     environment variable in your shell blocks python-dotenv from loading
#     the values from this file (load_dotenv never overrides). Remove them
#     from your environment or from the system env vars first.
#   * Free-tier gateways: a model listed by the gateway may still be
#     unavailable for your token group ("No available channel ... under
#     group X"). Test with curl before blaming RD-Agent.

# ==========================================
# Global configs
# ==========================================
MAX_RETRY=10
RETRY_WAIT_SECONDS=20

# LiteLLM backend (supports OpenAI / DeepSeek / Azure / gateways)
BACKEND=rdagent.oai.backend.LiteLLMAPIBackend

# Web UI (rdagent server_ui) requires an auth token in newer versions.
# After starting server_ui, open: http://localhost:19899/?token=<value below>
UI_SERVER_AUTH_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-token

# Optional: ask the LLM to write free-text content (hypotheses, analysis,
# feedback) in Simplified Chinese. Code and JSON field names stay in English.
# DEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT=You are an AI assistant who helps to answer user's questions. IMPORTANT: Always write all free-text content (hypotheses, analysis, feedback, summaries) in Simplified Chinese. Keep code, JSON field names, and variable names in English unchanged.

# ==========================================
# Setup A (validated): gateway chat + SiliconFlow embedding
# ==========================================
# Chat: any OpenAI-compatible gateway (self-hosted new-api, relay, etc.)
# through the deepseek provider's variable pair, which is isolated from
# the OPENAI_* namespace and therefore does not hijack the embedding route.
# The model name after `deepseek/` must be offered by your gateway.
# CHAT_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-flash
# DEEPSEEK_API_BASE=https://your-gateway.example.com/v1
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-your-gateway-api-key

# Embedding: SiliconFlow (BAAI/bge-m3 is free there; account balance must
# be positive even for free models).
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=litellm_proxy/BAAI/bge-m3
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY=sk-your-siliconflow-api-key
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_BASE=https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1

# ==========================================
# Setup B (validated): everything on SiliconFlow
# ==========================================
# Chat and embedding both use the litellm_proxy/ prefix against the same
# provider. DeepSeek-V3.2 (or any hosted model) for chat, BGE for embedding.
# CHAT_MODEL=litellm_proxy/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.2
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=litellm_proxy/BAAI/bge-m3
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_KEY=sk-your-siliconflow-api-key
# LITELLM_PROXY_API_BASE=https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1

# ==========================================
# Plain OpenAI (official)
# ==========================================
# CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# OPENAI_API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key

# ==========================================
# Azure OpenAI users
# ==========================================
# AZURE_API_KEY=
# AZURE_API_BASE=
# AZURE_API_VERSION=

# ==========================================
# Cache settings (optional, saves tokens on repeated calls)
# ==========================================
# USE_CHAT_CACHE=True
# USE_EMBEDDING_CACHE=True
# FT_DOCKER_ENABLE_CACHE=True
# DS_DOCKER_ENABLE_CACHE=True
